set-bg: img/map_2.jpg

= Fifth Emergency Decree for Economy and Finance

With the abolishment of War Loan payments and Askew's government surviving the intrigues of [? if president == "DuFour": DuFour's inner circle?][? if president != "DuFour": his supporting parties?] for the time being, Dietrich's public works program has officially been granted its full billion-crown funding!

This marks a real turning point, and along with the abolishment of War Loans, the radicalizing effects of sky-high unemployment and the Etaluxia Treaty are diminished. The set of conditions that have enabled the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> meteoric rise begins to unravel, depriving them of the fuel that once drove their ascent.

- @public_works

@public_works
title: The decree is signed into law by President [+ president +].
on-arrival: labor_dissent -= 20; wtb_points += 200; lautenbach_adopted = 1; lautenbach_plan_time = time + 12; dufour_angry_bruning -= 75; gold_left += 5; ddp_left += 3; lvp_left += 3; ddp_cohesion += 3; unionist_relation += 5 if wtb_adopted; ddp_relation += 5 if wtb_adopted; lvp_relation += 5 if wtb_adopted; inflation += 1; budget -= 2; economic_growth += 2; works_program += 1; commons_royalist -= 4; commons_ddp += 2; commons_unionist += 2; commons_lvp += 2; commons_kvp += 2; disfavored -= 3; disfavored_royalist -= 6; disfavored_unionist += 3; disfavored_ddp += 3; disfavored_lvp += 3; disfavored_kvp += 3

Despite Askew's belief that public works should come only after the economic calamity has bottomed out, it seems like he finally believes that it has done so, with a global recovery on the horizon after the abolishment in the Commonwealth's War Loans. The plan is similar to the previously proposed Larkmoor plan in many aspects, although with a more limited expansion of credit due to inflationary fears.

> Chancellor [+ chancellor +]'s response is, public works?